INSERT INTO public.intel_briefing_variants (briefing_id, depth, content_md) VALUES
  ('1ee1846c-f4c9-473c-a520-654a22a65aee', 1, 'Scammers evade detection by recycling social media accounts and wallets under new project names, but BlackBox Farm tracks immutable numeric IDs to expose these hidden histories. By mapping persistent identifiers and wallet reputations, the platform reveals past rug pulls that simple username searches miss.'),
  ('802ceff4-45a0-447c-b8e0-9a0be09239ee', 1, 'BlackBox Farm’s intelligence tools allow traders to mitigate risk by tracing a developer''s immutable on-chain history, including previous launches, funding sources, and reputation flags. Identifying repeat offenders and hidden exit strategies before buying is the most predictive signal for Solana due diligence.'),
  ('606a500a-d6aa-4ddc-84e3-5caede2cecb3', 1, 'Tracing a Solana token from its developer to the funding source and KYC root reveals the true identity and intent behind a project. BlackBox Farm automates this deep forensic analysis to expose professional serial ruggers who use fresh wallets to hide systematic patterns of extraction.'),
  ('4f603e56-a26d-4aa4-8c56-23ff45358e39', 1, 'BlackBox Farm’s KYC Root Tracing exposes the real identities behind anonymous Solana wallets by recursively scanning funding chains up to three levels deep. This advanced tool unmasks serial scammers and coordinated insider networks by linking fresh developer wallets to master exchange-connected accounts.'),
  ('ee86ac25-0e84-4173-935a-235d67c0f3f8', 1, 'Successful Solana trading relies on identifying recurring structural risks like supply concentration, hidden wallet clusters, and developer history. By cross-referencing holder data with liquidity depth and social patterns, traders can detect manipulation before a price collapse occurs.'),
  ('ce6df337-8e43-4fc3-8ec3-4600352cefd5', 1, 'BlackBox Farm''s Bubble Map is a visual intelligence tool that maps hidden connections between Solana tokens, developer histories, funding chains, and social identities. By tracing on-chain data and immutable social IDs, it exposes serial ruggers and insider clusters that traditional data lists miss. This interactive graph transforms complex forensics into readable patterns for superior due diligence.'),
  ('efa2d619-3a0b-4cd9-8285-e6c69f87ee5a', 1, 'The BlackBox Farm Bubble Map is an interactive network graph that visualizes relationships between Solana tokens, developers, and social links to detect fraud. By mapping on-chain funding origins and recycled social identities, traders can instantly identify serial ruggers and coordinated insider networks.'),
  ('bd20c6d2-5f88-4005-8083-c1f8f92f7ebc', 1, 'Wallet analysis tools look past surface-level price data to reveal true ownership concentration, hidden cluster relationships, and behavioral patterns. By filtering noise and identifying coordinated control, these tools expose the structural risks and causes behind market effects that charts cannot capture.'),
  ('c288871c-5ec2-466a-9c4c-c03677f25d9e', 1, 'Price charts are lagging indicators that mask the coordinated wallet behaviors driving market movements. Real edge requires wallet intelligence to uncover supply concentration, insider clusters, and deceptive holder metrics. BlackBox Farm provides this transparency through instant, AI-driven analysis of functional holder data to identify structural risks before they manifest in price.'),
  ('ed139f0e-0ef5-4b7e-8067-a7b5cc170fa2', 1, 'Rug pulls are engineered events with detectable on-chain signatures that appear long before the exit. Investors can identify these traps by monitoring supply concentration, hidden wallet clustering, and developer movements. Quantitative data reveals the structural setup that price charts alone cannot.'),
  ('e424b982-9cbb-4cda-baf1-6d34de9af8cf', 1, 'Successful Solana trading requires prioritizing holder analysis over technical charts to identify supply concentration and insider manipulation. BlackBox Farm provides the essential data to verify distribution, stability, and wallet reputation, ensuring traders avoid exit liquidity traps.'),
  ('2bb20acc-293f-4bfd-9b50-c0d0d9e6485b', 1, 'Bubble maps visualize the wallet networks of tokens to reveal who actually controls the supply, exposing hidden clusters and coordinated links that price charts and simple holder counts mask. By identifying interconnected nodes and centralized hubs, investors can distinguish genuine decentralization from manufactured distribution. This structural analysis provides a critical diagnosis of market health and potential manipulation before price action occurs.'),
  ('b2c9fab4-6b87-45a7-99f6-27cb35f61959', 1, 'Smart money operates through a strategic four-phase playbook of early accumulation, position splitting, narrative maintenance, and quiet distribution to maximize profits. Investors can overcome information asymmetry by using on-chain tools to track these hidden behavioral signatures before they manifest as lagging price signals.'),
  ('7ce72fb1-9c21-4740-8968-df1c1ed58884', 1, 'Successful token analysis prioritizes ownership structure over price charts to reveal the true causes of market movement. Investors must filter out dust wallets to identify functional holder counts, detect hidden clusters of coordinated addresses, and monitor developer activity for exit signals. Understanding these underlying power dynamics is essential for avoiding coordinated dumps and catastrophic rug pulls.'),
  ('7c86e302-4e40-4bb3-b11a-e357649042c3', 1, 'Holder distribution measures how token supply is spread across wallets, serving as a primary predictor for rug pulls. High concentration in a few unlabeled or coordinated wallets allows insiders to manipulate price and drain liquidity. Evaluating these patterns is essential to identifying structural risks.'),
  ('ab852680-76fa-4428-91e4-f12251aa4cb5', 1, 'Speed is a performance multiplier that accelerates losses when applied to noise instead of structural substance. Smart traders prioritize evaluating wallet distribution and network health over reacting to price momentum, ensuring entries are backed by sound data rather than traps. True timing advantages stem from analyzing conditions that precede market movements.'),
  ('a66888b8-f34e-4c89-876c-705b429806c2', 1, 'High liquidity facilitates efficient market entry but fails to account for exit risks driven by concentrated token ownership. Deep pools are often strategically seeded to mask insider control and coordinated wallet clusters. Investors must verify wallet distribution and structural data to distinguish a healthy market from a sophisticated retail trap.'),
  ('fb6a71c8-f1f0-42b0-99ad-654d1b490610', 1, 'Bad actors simulate decentralization by distributing concentrated supply across coordinated wallets to deceive retail investors. Detection requires structural analysis of hub-and-spoke funding patterns and synchronized wallet behavior. Use specialized tools to expose these cosmetic distributions and verify genuine ownership.'),
  ('8176bfa2-1daf-48e9-92bc-d06845410ca1', 1, 'Crypto trading volume is frequently manufactured through wash trading, micro-trade spam, and automated bots to engineer a false perception of market legitimacy. Genuine volume is distinguished by diverse trade sizes and shifting holder distributions. If high volume fails to improve token distribution or expand the participant base, it is an inorganic illusion rather than true market interest.'),
  ('b3d021dc-32f0-4067-82a1-6fe434f4b28c', 1, 'High holder counts are frequently manipulated through dust airdrops and wallet splitting to manufacture a false sense of community and decentralization. Investors must utilize functional holder analysis to filter out statistical noise and reveal the true distribution of supply. Identifying the actual number of meaningful, independent participants is essential to uncovering hidden concentration and avoiding predatory extraction.'),
  ('6f58d65c-bc03-426c-8776-34dc5339aad9', 1, 'Retail traders often lose money because they rely on easily manipulated metrics like price action and social hype. True market advantage comes from analyzing wallet structure—supply concentration, clustering, and developer behavior—to identify manufactured momentum and avoid providing exit liquidity.')
